# AutoLoot Implementation Task List

Proposal: [AutoLootProposal.md](./AutoLootProposal.md)
Status: Phases 1-4 complete; final automated validation and gameplay acceptance pending.

Conventions:
    [ ] Pending task.
    [x] Completed task with evidence or decisions recorded in the proposal.
    Each task has a stable ID and explicit prerequisites.
    "Depends: none" means the task can proceed independently.
    Implementation and automated tests precede in-game acceptance testing.
    The client-only API/protocol investigation is already complete for the
    inspected game version; do not treat a new feasibility investigation or
    in-game test of an unimplemented feature as a prerequisite.

## Design Constraints
    - Client-only AutoLoot; no custom server ModSystem, channel, or packets.
    - Use the normal vanilla corpse interaction and inventory-open lifecycle.
    - Send vanilla transfer packets through the corpse's entity-wrapped route.
    - Collect available loot only; never harvest, generate drops, or bypass access.
    - Transfer everything that fits; leave overflow intact on the corpse.
    - One collection pass per continuous hold, not one packet per hold.
    - Preserve normal click-to-open and all existing AutoStash behavior.
    - Treat hold duration and feature enablement as local UX preferences.
    - Do not present predicted movement as confirmed server success.
    - Initial scope is standard harvested corpses, not arbitrary entity storage.

## Phase 1: Resolve Integration Details
    [x] AL-01: Select the narrow client interaction hook.
        Depends: none.
        Inspect the existing interaction/input boundaries and choose how the
        gesture starts while allowing vanilla interaction to open the inventory.
        Account for held/released input after the loot dialog opens, including
        immersive mouse mode. Do not suppress the server's normal open flow.
        Prefer existing API hooks; use a client-only Harmony patch only if needed.
        Record the selected approach in the proposal.
        Completed 2026-10-18; revised to the user-requested VE-owned behavior:
        register EntityBehaviorAutoLootable and append its descriptor to matching
        synchronized client entity definitions at BlockTexturesLoaded, after
        existing behaviors, leaving vanilla opening/handling unchanged.
        Use raw button state plus non-consuming release observation, bind the
        gesture to the corpse/session while its window is open, and distinguish
        UI cursor movement from world retargeting. See proposal Phase 1 Decisions
        for inspected API/IL evidence and lifecycle guards.

    [x] AL-02: Finalize eligibility and presentation decisions.
        Depends: none.
        Confirm first-release eligibility as the standard harvested-corpse path;
        leave player corpses and other mod-specific inventory protocols excluded
        unless explicitly approved and verified.
        Decide whether AutoLoot exposes its own render-topmost preference or uses
        a documented default independent of AutoStash's setting.
        Define neutral completion/capacity feedback without an aggregate server
        acknowledgement or an inferred access-denied reason.
        Record these decisions in the proposal.
        Completed 2026-10-18: standard dead, harvested, non-player corpses with
        available loot and the vanilla-opened standard inventory/protocol only.
        User selected fixed topmost rendering without an additional setting and
        keeping the loot window open with a corpse-bound hold. Clear progress
        after dispatch/cancel; use existing inventory views for capacity/results,
        without predicted-success sounds/counts or inferred rejection messages.

## Phase 2: Share Hold and Progress Infrastructure
    [x] AL-03: Extract a small shared hold lifecycle with focused tests.
        Depends: none.
        Own elapsed time, grace-period visibility, clamped progress, label,
        cancellation, cleanup, and submit-once completion state.
        Keep input interpretation, target identity, eligibility, and dispatch in
        feature adapters. Preserve callback-driven and tick-driven callers.
        Test exact grace/completion thresholds, release/reset, repeated updates
        after completion, unavailable rendering, and idempotent cleanup.
        Avoid a general-purpose interaction framework.
        Completed 2026-10-18: HoldInteractionProgress owns absolute/delta timing,
        grace visibility, label, clamped progress, submit-once completion, and
        idempotent reset/removal. Focused tests cover exact boundaries, restart,
        overshoot, unavailable rendering/recovery, and cleanup failures.

    [x] AL-04: Decouple radial presentation from AutoStash configuration.
        Depends: AL-02.
        Allow callers to supply presentation preferences to progress creation.
        Preserve existing AutoStashGuiRendersTopmost configuration and behavior.
        Reuse IProgressSystemProvider, the current renderer, and existing shaders.
        Update directly affected callers, mocks, and progress tests.
        Completed 2026-10-18: CreateProgressBar accepts explicit rendersTopmost;
        the provider forwards it into radial creation without reading feature
        configuration. Feature-neutral radial defaults are topmost=true.
        Both AutoStash adapters pass their existing setting explicitly, with
        tests for true and false. AutoLoot can later pass fixed true.

    [x] AL-05: Migrate AutoStash callers to shared hold behavior.
        Depends: AL-03.
        Migrate attached-container timing/progress ownership first; adapt block
        interaction lifecycle where practical without forcing a shared input loop.
        Preserve crate modifiers, attachment selection, block handling, pre/post
        grace periods, animations, sounds, and current packet dispatch.
        Keep matching policies and the server transfer executor stash-specific.
        Run targeted block/attached-container interaction and lifecycle tests.
        Completed 2026-10-18: attached ticks and block elapsed callbacks now use
        the shared lifecycle; target/input policies and packet dispatch remain
        feature-owned. Completion keeps progress removed during the block's
        existing post-stash grace instead of recreating the completed indicator.
        Verified 436 focused unit tests and one isolated real-Harmony dispatch
        integration test; mod and test projects compile successfully.

## Phase 3: Implement Client AutoLoot
    [x] AL-06: Add a client-only feature lifecycle and corpse adapter.
        Depends: AL-01, AL-02.
        Resolve the current standard harvested corpse and its actual inventory.
        Require a dead, eligible target with available loot; track entity identity
        and the current vanilla-opened session rather than a copied inventory.
        Observe open/close and invalidation; local OpenInventory alone must never
        be treated as server authorization.
        Register only required client hooks/listeners and release them on disposal.
        Do not alter corpse drops, watched attributes, persistence, or cleanup.
        Completed: AutoLootSystem_Client owns client-only behavior registration,
        idempotent synchronized-definition amendment, tick/input/world listeners,
        live-disable handling,
        and disposal. AutoLootTarget binds the exact native harvestable behavior,
        corpse identity, real inventory/session, player, dimension, and hit point.
        Session, eligibility, and reach checks are read-only; vanilla alone opens
        and authorizes the session. Custom behavior subclasses are excluded.
        Client definitions with registered harvestable behavior classes, aliases,
        or subclasses receive the owned descriptor. The engine constructs and
        initializes it normally on cloned entity definitions; no per-instance
        scan/attachment listener remains. Only collection eligibility applies
        the exact-native restriction. Definition amendment is independent of the
        enable toggle so live enabling works. No AutoLoot Harmony patch remains.

    [x] AL-07: Add the vanilla client transfer coordinator.
        Depends: AL-06.
        Iterate current nonempty source slots using TryTransferAway with
        onlyPlayerInventory: true and the appropriate ActingPlayer/operation.
        Send each returned packet once via SendEntityPacketWithOffset using the
        target entity and the verified corpse packet offset.
        Do not also send an activate/shift-click packet for the same operation.
        Preserve engine merge rules, stack attributes, restrictions, and partial
        movement; never clone items and clear the source.
        Continue to later loot stacks when another stack cannot move.
        Stop on session/target invalidation and bound any additional retry loop.
        Use TryTransferTo only if exact destination routing proves necessary.
        Reuse client transfer prior art without extracting unused abstractions or
        routing corpse operations through global SendPacketClient.
        Completed: AutoLootTransferCoordinator makes one bounded source-slot pass
        using TryTransferAway with player-only destinations and ActingPlayer.
        Every returned packet is sent once to the bound entity with offset zero.
        No duplicate activation packets, manual source mutation, custom channel,
        or correction retries. Already-predicted packets are dispatched before
        stopping an invalidated pass; subsequent slots require a valid session.

    [x] AL-08: Wire the hold gesture to one collection pass.
        Depends: AL-03, AL-04, AL-06, AL-07.
        Start only for eligible corpses and let normal click-to-open proceed.
        Show localized radial progress after the grace period.
        At completion, require the valid vanilla-opened session before collecting;
        never substitute a locally forced open or an arbitrary readiness timeout.
        Cancel on release, world retargeting, lost reach, dimension change, closed
        session, target invalidation, focus loss, pause, disablement, or disposal.
        Keep the original corpse/session bound while its window is open; UI-only
        cursor movement is not retargeting. Observe release over the GUI without
        consuming vanilla input or relying solely on InWorldMouseButton.
        Require release before starting another pass after completion.
        Preserve existing windows; do not close an already-open loot inventory.
        Completed: appended owned behavior preserves original opening/handling and starts
        AutoLootClient's shared HoldInteractionProgress. Raw right-button polling
        and non-consuming MouseUp observation maintain a release latch, including
        over the GUI. The 0.1-second grace and configured delay use fixed topmost
        rendering. World/session/input invalidation removes progress without
        closing the loot window. Attached AutoStash takes precedence for a shared
        hold, cancelling pending loot until release without changing stash rules.
        Public OnInventoryClosed replaces private dialog access/subscriptions:
        local closure cancels immediately, another viewer closing does not.

    [x] AL-09: Implement prediction-aware feedback.
        Depends: AL-02, AL-07, AL-08.
        Distinguish neutral interaction completion from authoritative success.
        Use local capacity information cautiously and observe vanilla corrections;
        do not promise a confirmed collected count from predicted movement.
        Do not add custom result packets or automatic endless correction retries.
        Surface unexpected failures using existing logging conventions.
        Completed: progress ends at dispatch, not confirmed success. Existing
        inventory views and vanilla corrections provide results; no predicted
        counts, success sounds, or inferred full/access-denied messages are added.
        Unexpected collection/timing failures cancel and log the full exception.
        Initially verified 52 AutoLoot tests within 488 passing focused unit tests, plus
        one passing isolated AutoStash Harmony integration test. Tests include
        native corpse dispatch, lifecycle, transport, capacity/attributes,
        bounded invalidation, error logging, and cross-feature progress cleanup.
        No in-game or unmodified-server gameplay verification is claimed.

## Phase 4: Configuration, Localization, and Documentation
    [x] AL-10: Integrate local AutoLoot settings.
        Depends: AL-02, AL-06.
        Add EnableAutoLoot (default true) and AutoLootDelay (default 0.5 seconds).
        Follow existing delay validation/range conventions and ConfigLib patterns.
        Supply fixed topmost=true for AutoLoot without an additional setting or
        coupling to AutoStashGuiRendersTopmost.
        Verify ConfigLib does not turn these settings into a server dependency.
        Support independent AutoLoot/AutoStash enablement and cancel active work
        when AutoLoot is disabled.
        Keep the mod universal and requiredOnServer: false.
        Completed: both settings now have clientSide=true ConfigLib definitions
        in a dedicated Auto Loot section. EnableAutoLoot defaults true; delay
        defaults 0.5 seconds with the existing 0.1-2, step 0.1 slider convention.
        Shared timing validation rejects invalid manual delays with logging.
        ConfigLib 1.10.12 IL inspection confirms client-side values are preserved
        during server synchronization and ignored by server-setting updates.
        No required dependency or server code was added; the universal manifest
        retains requiredOnServer=false. Tests cover persistence/older files,
        exact delay thresholds, and all four ConfigLib event paths for immediate
        cancellation/re-enabling with AutoStash independently enabled or disabled.
        Fixed topmost rendering remains independent of AutoStash configuration.

