## Phase 5: Automated Validation
    [ ] AL-13: Cover gesture, session, and feature lifecycle behavior.
        Depends: AL-05, AL-08, AL-10.
        Use feature-organized tests and existing mocks; mark unit tests Category=Unit.
        Cover short click, timing boundaries, repeated ticks/interactions, release,
        retargeting, reach/dimension changes, empty/living/unharvested targets,
        delayed session readiness, session closure, disablement, and disposal.
        Assert at most one collection pass per hold and complete progress cleanup.
        Verify AutoLoot and AutoStash work independently and do not leave orphaned
        or overlapping indicators.

    [ ] AL-14: Cover transfer correctness and packet transport.
        Depends: AL-07, AL-09.
        Prefer real InventoryGeneric instances and existing test infrastructure.
        Cover sufficient/full/partial capacity, existing-stack merges, restricted
        slots, rejected moves, multiple loot types, and attribute preservation.
        Assert player-only destinations, no transfers into unrelated open
        containers, correct entity-wrapped routing, and one send per returned packet.
        Test invalidation during callbacks, bounded termination, and no duplicate
        activate-plus-move submissions.
        Verify predicted movement is not reported as confirmed server success.
        Unit tests do not substitute for vanilla server reconciliation tests.

    [ ] AL-15: Run targeted regression checks and build.
        Depends: AL-04, AL-05, AL-09, AL-10, AL-11, AL-12, AL-13, AL-14.
        Run AutoLoot, shared-progress, and affected AutoStash tests with one focused
        runner/filter where possible; include client transfer regressions if shared
        AlloyCalculator code changed.
        Run the existing mod build and relevant asset/configuration validation.
        Fix regressions caused by the change; expand suites only when warranted.

## Phase 6: In-Game Release Acceptance (After Implementation)
    [ ] AL-16: Validate normal interaction and full/partial collection.
        Depends: AL-15.
        Test ordinary and immersive mouse modes in a running game.
        Confirm a click opens loot normally and holding survives dialog opening,
        displays progress, collects once, and requires release to repeat.
        Test release/retarget/cancel, inventory full, partial space, empty corpses,
        and intact harvesting requirements.
        Confirm AutoStash gestures and rendering remain unchanged.

    [ ] AL-17: Confirm operation against a server without VanillaExpanded.
        Depends: AL-15.
        Install the feature on the client only and connect to a compatible server
        without the mod. Confirm collection works and persists after reopening
        the corpse inventory and reconnecting.
        Verify no custom AutoLoot channel, packet handler, or server setting is
        required and other clients observe the updated corpse contents.

    [ ] AL-18: Validate latency, contention, and lifecycle edge cases.
        Depends: AL-15.
        Test two players looting the same corpse, delayed synchronization, rejected
        or stale predictions, session closure, target disappearance, and lost reach.
        Confirm vanilla reconciliation restores correct contents without item
        duplication, loss, endless retries, or false confirmed-success feedback.
        Confirm feature disablement and world exit leave no listeners or renderers.

    [ ] AL-19: Record acceptance results and close implementation tasks.
        Depends: AL-16, AL-17, AL-18.
        Record tested client/server versions, settings, outcomes, and limitations
        in the proposal or existing test documentation.
        Mark tasks complete only with corresponding implementation/test evidence.
        Leave unsupported corpse protocols explicitly out of scope.
